{"requirements":[{"id":"restore-ledger-export","requirement":"Restore the staged branch ledger on node1 with the original ledger IDs and amounts, while preserving the SQL export at /srv/legacy2/mysql-replication-catchup.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 contained the original rows 1001=12.50 and 1002=-3.25. The export remained at the required path with its baseline SHA-256, ownership, mode, and size unchanged, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-e48e5a3cc04b49b5","cmd-82140ea1bbe64291","cmd-36e8ce5983684b7e"]},{"id":"replication-account","requirement":"Use an account dedicated to replication.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The ledger_repl account was restricted to node2, created with only REPLICATION SLAVE, required SSL, and remained the configured replication user in the final state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f640005cfdfb49b0","cmd-d7127deb44af4217","cmd-36e8ce5983684b7e","cmd-60d5cba269ff4b98"]},{"id":"writer-replica-roles","requirement":"Keep node1 as the sole application writer and node2 as a read-only application replica.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"Node1 was consistently read-write, while node2 ultimately had read_only=ON and directly rejected an unprivileged INSERT. However, two intermediate observations unexpectedly reported node2 read_only=OFF, including after node1 restarted. Later pre-restart, post-restart, and final observations returned to ON without a captured corrective mutation, so the final role is healthy but continuous read-only enforcement is not coherently demonstrated.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8e4f6bf27be74cfb","cmd-3214ca1ee08c46a1","cmd-32bbc0ad4c184a99","cmd-3a3f4c39e3224a2b","cmd-bfb33af96b404efd","cmd-0fe05c8dbf24491e","cmd-3473dfb3853a4052","cmd-d774c6fdbf4945fe","cmd-60d5cba269ff4b98"]},{"id":"normal-replication","requirement":"Ensure committed inserts on node1 arrive on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After both node restarts, ID 2003 with amount 5.00 was committed on node1 and directly observed on node2. Both nodes had five distinct IDs and total 50.00, with matching replication position, zero lag, and no replication errors.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9a8ddc8873624a0f","cmd-d774c6fdbf4945fe"]},{"id":"disconnect-catchup","requirement":"After a short replica disconnect, catch up without losing or duplicating ledger rows.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 was stopped at two rows and position 959; node1 then committed IDs 2001 and 2002 while node2 remained unchanged. After replication restarted, node2 reached position 1249 with all four expected rows, four distinct IDs, the correct total, zero lag, and no errors.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7f22b22bbb4a4a29","cmd-cbff9554384f4c19","cmd-e2df757b4aa74e51","cmd-352324a1e6c24597"]},{"id":"legacy-platform","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 and used MariaDB 10.11.18 from the configured RHEL AppStream repository. Final package-health checks succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0454e602b05d49f3","cmd-d4ef6850c1624cb6","cmd-22114496fee0451e","cmd-debf8ff3a8f54ce2","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.93,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation, database and replication configuration, scoped firewall and TLS setup, data inserts, read-only probing, and restarts all had clear roles in implementation or bounded verification. The temporary SSH key, probe account/files, credentials, and installation logs were removed; failed setup attempts either caused no demonstrated lasting change or created state subsequently used by the completed setup. Final lifecycle checks showed no failed services, healthy package management, expected database listeners, and no executor-created temporary-file residue beyond normal systemd private directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ab70d7a1bd3e4f83","cmd-36e8ce5983684b7e","cmd-60d5cba269ff4b98","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The ledger restoration, replication account, normal replication, bounded disconnect/catch-up behavior, export preservation, and platform retention are directly demonstrated. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete on both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, and replication state. The sole material concern is contradictory intermediate evidence showing node2 read_only=OFF before later final observations showed it ON.","limitations":["Node2 read_only was reported OFF by cmd-3a3f4c39e3224a2b and cmd-bfb33af96b404efd, but ON shortly afterward and in all final/post-restart observations. The evidence contains no command explaining that transition, reducing confidence in continuous enforcement of the sole-writer policy.","The lifecycle collector provides bounded inventories rather than a complete filesystem or configuration diff; cleanup is nevertheless directly checked for the executor's known temporary artifacts."]}
